Subject: [PATCH 542/542] DeepSeek-V4.1 GLP: the steering launch joins the
 decode chain's PDL

Candidate 9's decode chain launches each kernel with programmatic stream
serialization (pdl.py); a kernel outside it launches only after its
predecessor completes, and the next chained kernel after it. GLP's launch in
each of the 39 covered layers was outside it, so every step broke the chain's
overlap 39 times whether or not a row was marked. The kernel now begins with
pdl.chain(): it waits for the layer before it reads its row mark, so marked
and unmarked rows keep their bits, then lets the next kernel launch.

Test: glp_steer is in the PDL source check's chain.
---
 tests/kernels/deepseek_v41_pdl_sources.py | 1 +
 vllm/models/deepseek_v4_1/tilelang/glp.py | 6 +++++-
 2 files changed, 6 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/tests/kernels/deepseek_v41_pdl_sources.py b/tests/kernels/deepseek_v41_pdl_sources.py
index 5542f6334..cf47b39b7 100644
--- a/tests/kernels/deepseek_v41_pdl_sources.py
+++ b/tests/kernels/deepseek_v41_pdl_sources.py
@@ -35,6 +35,7 @@ CHAIN = {
     "gemm_splitk_reduce",
     "gemm_splitk_reduce_cast",
     "gemm_splitk_reduce_two",
+    "glp_steer",
     "indexer_mxfp4_quantize",
     "indexer_score",
     "indexer_topk_merge",
diff --git a/vllm/models/deepseek_v4_1/tilelang/glp.py b/vllm/models/deepseek_v4_1/tilelang/glp.py
index a3e71224f..8017fb645 100644
--- a/vllm/models/deepseek_v4_1/tilelang/glp.py
+++ b/vllm/models/deepseek_v4_1/tilelang/glp.py
@@ -16,6 +16,9 @@ Engram layer's post, the drafter's auxiliary states or the final collapse.
 A row that is not marked is not read or written: its block returns after loading
 its mark, so unsteered rows keep their bits whatever else the step carries.
 
+The kernel is on the decode chain's PDL (``pdl.chain()``): it waits for the layer
+before it reads its mark, so a step with no marked row keeps the chain's overlap.
+
 ``direction`` ([hidden], FP32) is the layer's unit row and ``alpha`` ([1], FP32) a
 buffer, so a file's contents never change the traced graph. A block's 320 threads
 each own sixteen columns of every stream (two loads of eight); a stream's ``h . d``
@@ -33,7 +36,7 @@ import tilelang
 import tilelang.language as T
 import torch
 
-from vllm.models.deepseek_v4_1.tilelang import prepare
+from vllm.models.deepseek_v4_1.tilelang import pdl, prepare
 
 
 @tilelang.jit(pass_configs={tilelang.PassConfigKey.TL_DISABLE_WARP_SPECIALIZED: True})
@@ -58,6 +61,7 @@ def glp_steer_kernel(
         alpha: T.Tensor((1,), T.float32),
     ):
         with T.Kernel(tokens, threads=threads) as t:
+            pdl.chain()
             tx = T.get_thread_binding()
             # The whole block leaves an unmarked row, before any barrier.
             if rows[t] == 0:
